+j = b^3/c^2.
+```
+
+See `pi1s4-64-zvk-u6-opus5-20260831.md:154-163`. Singular parameter pairs have
+`t != s`, `r(t)=+-r(s)`, and `q(t)=q(s)`, with `e=t+s`, `p=ts`
+(`...zvk-u6...:94-103`). The minus branch is empty for `c != 0`; the plus branch
+is exactly
+
+```text
+h(e) = e^3 + (4b/3)e - 4c/3 = 0,       p = e^2 + b.
+```
+
