+T^2 - eT + (e^2+b) = 0,             (1)
+```
+
+and `h(e)=0`. The pair discriminant is
+
+```text
+(t-s)^2 = e^2 - 4(e^2+b) = -3e^2 - 4b.             (2)
+```
+
+If `3e^2+4b=0`, then `h(e)=e(e^2+4b/3)-4c/3=-4c/3`, impossible because
+`c != 0`. Thus every plus solution has two distinct parameters.
